1. A chat stream that ends without a finish_reason, or with finish_reason
   error, ends in a RUN_ERROR (code incomplete-stream) instead of finishing
   as stop or content_filter. That RUN_ERROR, and the one the catch reports,
   carry the usage the stream reported before it failed. Upstream PR to be
   opened; remove when released.
2. The terminal event carries the choice's finish_reason as
   metadata.providerStopReason, so the service decides every finish reason from
   the SDK's union (apps/api/src/lib/chat/provider-stop-reasons.ts) instead
   of reading an unhandled one as "stop". Remove when upstream exposes the
   raw reason.


